<title>HONG KONG: China Airlines orders Airbus A300-600.</title>
<headline>China Airlines orders Airbus A300-600.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taipei-based China Airlines has placed an order with Airbus Industrie for the purchase of an additional twin engine widebody A300-600 aircraft, Airbus said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The aircraft will be delivered in the first quarter of 1999, Airbus said in a statement received in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Airbus said the aircraft is the fifteenth to be ordered by China Airlines, which operates a combination of A300B4s and A300-600s on its Asian network.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
